 that you actually put it out online.

302
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:10,980
 It's the reason why you're running to your buddies

303
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:13,480
 and you're asking them, hey, how did that thing sound?

304
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,880
 When in reality, they've already told you that it was good.

305
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:19,620
 It's the reason why you walk into a conversation

306
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:21,060
 and it's not even about you,

307
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:23,860
 and yet it somehow ends up being about you.

308
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:26,500
 It's why when you're in an argument and you're 90% wrong,

309
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,400
 somehow the 10% that is right

310
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:31,660
 ends up being the very last word that is extended.

311
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:36,580
 We know that for many of us, we struggle with pride,

312
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:39,300
 that our lives are living to tell the greatness of us

313
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,140
 instead of the greatness of God.

314
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:43,480
 And that's a really dangerous quality to carry.

315
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:46,140
 The reason why is because we read this

316
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:49,140
 about God's position on pride in James 4:6.

317
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:50,620
 This is just one verse, there's many,

318
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:52,340
 but for the sake of time, I'll give you one.

319
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:54,240
 It says, "God opposes," or the Greek there

320
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:57,340
 is also the idea of he resists the proud,

321
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:59,780
 but he gives grace to the humble.

322
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:02,500
 A good way of thinking about this is the same way

323
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:05,900
 that in the Revolutionary War,

324
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:08,460
 when people would draw battle lines,

325
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:10,380
 one group of men would stand across the field

326
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:11,220
 from another group of men,

327
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:13,940
 and they would take turns shooting at each other.

328
00:13:13,940 --> 00:13:15,740
 You know what I'm talking about?

329
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:20,140
 In the same way, God has lined up against you, proud man,

330
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:22,960
 and yet though you may have a musket, he has a tank.

331
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,220
 It's not gonna end well for you.

332
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,300
 Like he opposes you, he resists you.

333
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:29,660
 That's the idea that's being communicated by way of James.

334
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:31,740
 So why the heck do we do this?

335
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:35,220
 Like if this is the heart of God with respect to the proud,

336
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:39,340
 why is it that we continue to function in pride?

337
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:40,820
 Because pride is very tricky.

338
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,700
 The first thing you gotta know about

339
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:45,480
 is that pride starts out as insecurity.

340
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,900
 Pride starts as insecurity.

341
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:48,400
 That's what we see in the first character

342
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,340
 we're gonna look at tonight.

343
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:52,340
 We see this in the life of King Saul.

344
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,540
 We meet him in 1 Samuel 10.

345
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:55,740
 We're gonna be in different passages all over the place.

346
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:57,580
 You can try and Bible bowl your way around

347
00:13:57,580 --> 00:13:58,420
 and keep up if you want,

348
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,740
 but they'll be on the screens.

349
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:01,900
 1 Samuel 10 says this.

350
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:03,700
 It says in verse 22,

351
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:06,340
 "So they inquired again to the Lord,

352
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:08,020
 "is there a man still to come?"

353
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:09,700
 You see, this is a group of people

354
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:12,900
 that were awaiting for God's appointed representative,

355
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:16,120
 his appointed king, to be identified.

356
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:19,280
 And yet it reads that behold,

357
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:21,580
 that guy has hidden himself among the baggage.

358
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:24,900
 Gentlemen, some of you have hidden yourself

359
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:26,820
 in the baggage here tonight.

360
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:28,740
 You are like King Saul.

361
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:32,300
 You have put yourself in a place where you are now hidden,

362
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:35,980
 hiding among the baggage because you're insecure.

363
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:39,220
 Like that's what happens with those that suffer in pride.

364
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:42,020
 We snap into self-preservation mode.

365
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:43,660
 Why is Saul hiding in the baggage?

366
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:44,820
 He's hiding in the baggage

367
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:48,260
 because he's afraid of failing as Israel's first king.

368
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:50,000
 That's a really big job.

369
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,060
 And yet he didn't ask for it.

370
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:54,980
 And because he doesn't have the confidence in himself

371
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:58,620
 to do the work, he chooses instead to hide himself away.

372
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:00,300
 You see, this is interesting

373
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:01,380
 because when we think of pride,

374
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:04,180
 we often think about the guy that like puffs his chest out,

375
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:06,780
 doesn't need help, never cries about anything.

376
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,780
 And yet pride can also be just as true for the guy

377
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:11,860
 whose chest is caved in.

378
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,380
 Because here's the thing,

379
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:15,740
 insecurity looks a lot like humility,

380
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,340
 but they have nothing in common.

381
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:19,560
 That's why some of you,

382
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:23,060
 you struggle to celebrate other people's success.

383
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:25,860
 It's why others of you,

384
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:28,660
 you'll get 10 compliments for what a great job you did,

385
00:15:28,660 --> 00:15:31,540
 but it's the one criticism that lives in your mind

386
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:34,700
 and reigns supreme over all your thoughts.

387
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:36,220
 It's why you'll ask friends

388
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:38,260
 if you made the right decision or not.

389
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:40,780
 It's why you go from one relationship to another

390
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:45,100
 because the validation of God in your life is not enough.

391
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:47,860
 You need the validation of other people, of other things.

392
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:50,700
 And so you run to them instead.

393
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,740
 But that's not all pride does.

394
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:52,900
 The second thing that you have to know about pride

395
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:55,620
 is that pride thinks it knows better than God.

396
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:57,300
 Pride thinks it knows better than God.

397
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:59,020
 Like in just a couple of chapters later

398
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,920
 from 1 Samuel chapter 10, when we meet King Saul,

399
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,740
 we see King Saul in battle.

400
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:06,580
 And what we realize is he starts off strong.

401
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:08,260
 Like he begins to have some success.

402
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:11,900
 And yet in chapter 13, when he's supposed to wait on Samuel,

403
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:14,220
 the prophet to come and to offer a sacrifice

404
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:16,940
 so that way they can go into war against the Philistines,

405
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:20,300
 Samuel's late, according to Saul's estimation.

406
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:23,320
 And so he does what he thinks is best.

407
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:25,300
 Like he knows the Philistines are coming.

408
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,620
 My army is scattering, time is expiring.

409
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:32,500
 And so he goes ahead and he sacrifices

410
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,340
 in order to prepare his people for battle.

411
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:38,420
 And yet, instead of trusting God,

412
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,860
 he trusts his own discernment.

413
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:42,660
 He does what he believes to be right.

414
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:44,580
 And it actually is wrong instead.

415
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,900
 It's funny.

416
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:51,740
 This idea of pride thinking it knows better than God

417
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:54,860
 is actually something that is proliferate among men.

418
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:55,800
 And I've experienced this,

419
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,060
 I've interacted with different guys.

420
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:58,580
 I remember when I lived in Houston,

421
00:16:58,580 --> 00:16:59,660
 there was a guy who came up to me

422
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:03,520
 and he wanted to justify his desire

423
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,820
 for masturbation and marijuana.

424
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:08,180
 And I remember looking at him and asking what his case was.

425
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:09,460
 And his case was a really simple case.

426
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,060
 He came in, the Bible doesn't explicitly talk

427
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:11,900
 about either one of those.

428
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:13,340
 It doesn't declare that either of them

429
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:15,680
 are specifically wrong.

430
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,820
 And I looked at him in response.

431
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:17,700
 I was like, well, brother,

432
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,420
 the Bible also does not specifically say

433
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:20,840
 that 90 day fiance is wrong,

434
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:23,420
 but we can both agree that that is not a good thing.

435
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:25,420
 We knew in that moment

436
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,740
 that he was doing what man should not do.

437
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:32,540
 He was trying to impose his will upon the word of God.

438
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:36,460
 He was trying to mold God's word to fit his life

439
00:17:36,460 --> 00:17:39,820
 as opposed to fit his life into God's word.

440
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:44,100
 And to do such a thing is a very proud thing to do.

441
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:48,420
 Deuteronomy 4.2 tells us do not add to what I command you.

442
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,900
 Don't subtract from it,

443
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:53,020
 but keep the commands of the Lord your God that I give you.

444
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,580
 Another thing that you need to know

445
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,700
 in the battle against pride

446
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:58,340
 is that pride sends other people to fight our battles.

447
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:03,060
 That's what Saul does with David in 1 Samuel 17.

448
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:06,540
 Like in a moment when the king of Israel,

449
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:09,380
 the tallest, broadest, strongest guy

450
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:11,580
 should walk into the valley of Elah

451
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:14,020
 and he should risk his life to deliver his people.

452
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:18,180
 He instead chooses to risk David's life, a shepherd boy.

453
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:20,300
 And the reason why is because pride,

454
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:21,540
 it says something interesting.

455
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:24,380
 Pride treats you as the most important person in the room.

456
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:25,700
 And because that is the case,

457
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:28,580
 it will sacrifice other people to protect you.

458
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:32,460
 That's why you'll joke at the expense of other people

459
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:33,700
 to make yourself feel good.

460
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,980
 It's why you will pressure your girlfriend into sex

461
00:18:35,980 --> 00:18:37,400
 because that feels good.

462
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,100
 It's why you'll force your future kids

463
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:41,180
 to play whatever sport you want them to play

464
00:18:41,180 --> 00:18:42,540
 because that feels good.

465
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:45,540
 This is what proud men do.

466
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,820
 They send other people to fight their battles.

467
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:52,820
 You wonder who sends other people to fight their battles

468
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:54,820
 according to the scripture?

469
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:57,740
 Not kings, cowards.

470
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:03,260
 It's what pride turned King Saul into.

471
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:04,900
 And that's what pride is trying to turn

472
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,020
 some of us into as well.

473
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,420
 And then lastly, you need to know this.

474
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:11,720
 Pride turns friends into enemies.

475
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:17,940
 At the end of his reign, all Saul did was envy David.

476
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:21,620
 And it was crazy when you consider what David did for Saul.

477
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:26,580
 Like David was his son's best friend.

478
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:29,520
 David had delivered the people from Goliath.

479
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:31,900
 David was even ministering to Saul

480
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:33,720
 in the midst of his own suffering.

481
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:37,340
 And yet Saul envied him nonetheless.

482
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:40,500
 And the reason why he did and the reason why we do this too

483
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:42,800
 is because manhood is measured in our world

484
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:46,460
 by how much you achieve, how much money you make,

485
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,420
 how high you can climb on the corporate ladder,

486
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:49,700
 how much influence you have,

487
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:51,540
 how many girls you've been with.

488
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:54,300
 And whenever we see another guy who has more,

489
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:57,660
 it often feels like a threat to our legitimacy as a man.

490
00:19:57,660 --> 00:20:02,300
 But according to Jesus, your manhood is not measured

491
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:05,420
 by how much you have.

492
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:07,220
 It is measured by how much you give.

493
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:10,100
 Because listen to me, and this is big.

494
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:13,640
 Pride might turn friends into enemies,

495
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,620
 but Jesus turns enemies into friends.

496
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:21,460
 He does what proud men never do.

497
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:25,500
 He gives of himself for the benefit of other people

498
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:28,060
 as opposed to taking from other people

499
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,700
 for the benefit of himself.

500
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:34,280
 Now, with all that said, because we gotta keep rolling,

501
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:36,900
 I do feel the need to just tell you a couple of steps

502
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:39,420
 on how you can begin to battle against pride

503
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:40,860
 in your own life if this is something

504
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,020
 that you're resonating with.

505
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:44,100
 If you're sitting here and you're like, dude, this is me,

506
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:45,660
 I don't wanna admit it 'cause I'm proud,

507
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:47,260
 but this is totally me.

508
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:48,860
 Like, I'm struggling with this right now.

509
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:50,820
 I can look in my life and I can see the ways

510
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:52,420
 that I've operated in insecurity.

511
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:54,860
 I know the fact that I have subjected other people

512
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:57,740
 to the public ridicule of my friends

513
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:59,420
 because it actually makes me look good.

514
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,220
 I've torn people down to build myself up.

515
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:03,140
 I can look at all different areas of my life

516
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:05,420
 and I can see the way in which this is true.

517
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:07,420
 Kylan, what do I do?

518
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:10,540
 I would give you three ways, three steps you can take.

519
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:14,420
 The first one is you can worship, you can worship.

520
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:16,620
 And the reason why worship is a really great step to take

521
00:21:16,620 --> 00:21:19,900
 is because worship is not about you.

522
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:22,460
 But here's the thing.

523
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,980
 I'm convinced that many men struggle to worship

524
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:30,620
 because they actually think it is about them.

525
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:34,460
 The way that you function in worship

526
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,620
 is you don't wanna look dumb, you don't wanna sound dumb,

527
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:39,740
 and so what you end up doing is the dumbest thing.

528
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:43,300
 You end up making the entire set

529
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,460
 about what people think of you

530
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:46,860
 rather than what people think of God.

531
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:48,620
 That's not what worship is.

532
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:51,620
 Worship is about King Jesus, not King you.

533
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:53,500
 And so the best thing you can do

534
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:56,580
 is you can worship like you actually mean it.

535
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:59,500
 I think about some of the manliest men in the scripture,

536
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:01,500
 and you wanna know the way that they worship?

537
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:04,380
 David danced indignantly before God.

538
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:07,220
 Think about the fact that the people of Israel

539
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:10,780
 would regularly raise hands

540
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:13,540
 and raise a joyful noise to the Lord.

541
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,940
 What if this was true?

542
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:18,700
 What if the truest thing about the worship experience

543
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:21,340
 here at The Porch was not

544
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,340
 that the bass from our speakers was loud,

545
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:26,980
 but the bass of our men's voice was louder?

546
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:28,700
 What if that was actually true?

547
00:22:28,700 --> 00:22:31,180
 What if you felt the worship in the room

548
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:33,420
 because the men sitting side by side

549
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:36,140
 were singing loudly to the glory of God

550
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:37,460
 as opposed to the glory of themselves?

551
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:39,500
 That's the first thing you can do.

552
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:41,580
 The second thing is you can fast.

553
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:45,700
 You can fast, and I do mean you can go without food.

554
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:47,340
 I'm not talking about one of those other kind of cheap fasts

555
00:22:47,340 --> 00:22:48,820
 where it's like, I'm gonna fast from social media,

556
00:22:48,820 --> 00:22:51,100
 I'm gonna fast from my television.

557
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,540
 I'm talking about the legitimate kind of fast,

558
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:56,300
 the fast where you actually deprive yourself of nourishment.

559
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:57,140
 Because here's the thing,

560
00:22:57,140 --> 00:22:59,220
 there's no quicker way to realize that you're not the man

561
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:00,700
 than to go 24 hours without food

562
00:23:00,700 --> 00:23:04,100
 and see just how quick you turn into a little whiny baby.

563
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:05,620
 Fasting humbles you.

564
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:07,020
 Like you might, I've seen it.

565
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:08,740
 You might bench 400 pounds,

566
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:10,620
 but you miss your bowl of Cheerios in the morning

567
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:13,020
 and you're less than the perfect version of yourself.

568
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:15,740
 That's the kind of impact that food actually has

569
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:17,100
 in the life of a person.

570
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:18,740
 Fasting proves how weak we are.

571
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:20,360
 That's why we should do it.

572
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:22,940
 It should remind us that we're not the one who is strong.

573
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:24,580
 God is the one who is strong.

574
00:23:24,580 --> 00:23:28,220
 Because while we depend on other things for life,

575
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:32,980
 life depends on God himself.

576
00:23:32,980 --> 00:23:34,100
 And then the third thing that I would tell you

577
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:35,780
 is you should pray.

578
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:37,420
 You should pray.

579
00:23:37,420 --> 00:23:39,700
 Like some of you, you need to do this.

580
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:42,820
 You need to come down here at the end of the service

581
00:23:42,820 --> 00:23:47,220
 and you need to tell God you need his help.

582
00:23:47,220 --> 00:23:49,360
 You need his help with your job

583
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,940
 and you need his help with your family.

584
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:52,580
 You need his help with your addiction.

585
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:54,240
 You need his help with your dreams

586
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:56,260
 and you need his help with your confusion

587
00:23:56,260 --> 00:23:57,980
 and your mental troubles.

588
00:23:57,980 --> 00:24:00,660
 And you need his help with respect to your relationship.

589
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:02,620
 I don't know what it is you need his help with,

590
00:24:02,620 --> 00:24:03,460
 but he knows.

591
00:24:03,460 --> 00:24:05,660
 He's just waiting for you to come and tell him,

592
00:24:05,660 --> 00:24:10,160
 to humble yourself and talk to him about it.

593
00:24:10,160 --> 00:24:12,260
 That's why every Tuesday we open this space

594
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:13,580
 and we have a team down front.

595
00:24:13,580 --> 00:24:14,940
 And tonight they will be here too,

596
00:24:14,940 --> 00:24:17,220
 ready for you to take that step.

597
00:24:17,220 --> 00:24:19,140
 Verse Peter 5, six through seven says,

598
00:24:19,140 --> 00:24:22,420
 humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of God

599
00:24:22,420 --> 00:24:24,760
 so that at the proper time he might exalt you,

600
00:24:24,760 --> 00:24:28,460
 casting all your anxieties on him because he cares for you.

601
00:24:28,460 --> 00:24:30,020
 We gotta humble ourselves, men.

602
00:24:30,020 --> 00:24:32,340
 Pride will demand recognition,

603
00:24:32,340 --> 00:24:34,980
 but Christ embraces humiliation.

604
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:36,920
 Pride protects reputation,

605
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:40,020
 but Jesus laid down his reputation

606
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,820
 and considered himself nothing.

607
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:43,940
 And where pride fears losing anything,

608
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:46,380
 Jesus lost everything for our sake.

609
00:24:46,380 --> 00:24:49,180
 You wanna know how to be humble?

610
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:52,700
 Look to that man and you will see the way.

611
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:53,540
 That's one.

612
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:55,900
 Two, second battle you need to know you'll face

613
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:57,720
 is the battle against anger.

614
00:24:57,720 --> 00:25:02,700
 On average, men are more likely to express their distress

615
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:06,520
 externally through anger and aggression and risk-taking,

616
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:09,240
 while women are more likely to express their distress

617
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:12,840
 internally through anxiety and sadness and worry.

618
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,140
 This is why, gentlemen,

619
00:25:14,140 --> 00:25:19,140
 when your team begins to struggle, you yell at the TV.

620
00:25:19,140 --> 00:25:21,320
 You don't know how else to express yourself.

621
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:22,580
 And ladies, this is why you cry

622
00:25:22,580 --> 00:25:23,860
 whenever you feel overwhelmed.

623
00:25:23,860 --> 00:25:24,940
 We're built different.

624
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:26,540
 Now, it's important to say this.

625
00:25:26,540 --> 00:25:31,740
 Anger as an emotion is not sinful.

626
00:25:31,740 --> 00:25:33,260
 Anger as an emotion is not sinful.

627
00:25:33,260 --> 00:25:34,140
 In fact, it's inevitable.

628
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:36,540
 Even Jesus experienced anger.

629
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:39,340
 So when then does anger become sinful?

630
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:43,540
 When your anger is not in defense of someone else,

631
00:25:43,540 --> 00:25:45,240
 it is in defense of yourself.

632
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:48,380
 That's when it becomes sinful.

633
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,580
 So listen to me.

634
00:25:49,580 --> 00:25:54,220
 If you get upset about the injustice

635
00:25:54,220 --> 00:25:57,240
 some other person is facing,

636
00:25:57,240 --> 00:26:01,500
 some indignity done against somebody else,

637
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:02,820
 you should be.

638
00:26:02,820 --> 00:26:04,560
 That's a good thing to be angry about.

639
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:07,640
 That's a good thing to feel a righteous indignation towards.

640
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:11,060
 Like we need men who actually feel that way,

641
00:26:11,060 --> 00:26:13,660
 who will run to help the innocent,

642
00:26:13,660 --> 00:26:16,500
 who will race into the fray,

643
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:19,540
 who will rally their brothers towards the cause of Christ,

644
00:26:19,540 --> 00:26:21,500
 wherever the cause of Christ is not represented.

645
00:26:21,500 --> 00:26:23,020
 We need you to feel that.

646
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:24,980
 Jesus felt that.

647
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:30,460
 But if you get upset because someone disagrees

648
00:26:30,460 --> 00:26:33,380
 with your political position online,

649
00:26:33,380 --> 00:26:35,460
 or someone cuts you off in traffic,

650
00:26:35,460 --> 00:26:37,300
 or someone unintentionally hurts your feelings,

651
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:39,160
 or someone offers you feedback,

652
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:41,080
 then that anger is sinful.

653
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:43,020
 Righteous anger, hear me on this,

654
00:26:43,020 --> 00:26:46,180
 righteous anger is a response to evil.

655
00:26:46,180 --> 00:26:50,540
 Unrighteous anger is a response to ego.

656
00:26:50,540 --> 00:26:55,140
 That's what we learned from our guy Moses.

657
00:26:55,140 --> 00:26:57,620
 It's funny, when you read Moses' story,

658
00:26:57,620 --> 00:26:59,620
 you see he's got a little bit of an anger issue.

659
00:26:59,620 --> 00:27:01,060
 There's two moments that stand out

660
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:03,580
 really strongly above the rest,

661
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:04,900
 where he expresses his anger.

662
00:27:04,900 --> 00:27:05,900
 One is a righteous moment,

663
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:06,900
 and one is an unrighteous moment.

664
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:08,580
 The righteous moment is when he

665
00:27:08,580 --> 00:27:10,180
 smashes the Ten Commandments.

666
00:27:10,180 --> 00:27:12,380
 Like he breaks the two tablets

667
00:27:12,380 --> 00:27:16,060
 because he sees the evil and idolatry

668
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:19,100
 of the people of God as they worship the golden calf.

669
00:27:19,100 --> 00:27:22,660
 That's a good and righteous anger.

670
00:27:22,660 --> 00:27:26,660
 The unrighteous anger that we see of Moses

671
00:27:26,660 --> 00:27:28,420
 is found in Numbers chapter 20.

672
00:27:28,420 --> 00:27:30,300
 And this is what it says.

673
00:27:30,300 --> 00:27:32,500
 Then Moses and Aaron gathered the assembly

674
00:27:32,500 --> 00:27:34,340
 together before the rock.

675
00:27:34,340 --> 00:27:35,220
 And he said to them,

676
00:27:35,220 --> 00:27:36,780
 "Hear now, you rebels.

677
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:39,660
 "Shall we bring water for you out of this rock?"

678
00:27:39,660 --> 00:27:40,980
 And Moses lifted up his hand,

679
00:27:40,980 --> 00:27:42,380
 and he struck the rock with his staff,

680
00:27:42,380 --> 00:27:44,220
 not once, but twice.

681
00:27:44,220 --> 00:27:45,720
 And water came out abundantly,

682
00:27:45,720 --> 00:27:48,500
 and the congregation drank in their livestock.

683
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:49,600
 And the Lord said to Moses and Aaron,

684
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:51,560
 "Because you didn't believe in me,

685
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:55,220
 "to uphold me as holy in the eyes of the people of Israel,

686
00:27:55,220 --> 00:27:57,280
 "therefore you shall not bring this assembly

687
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:59,660
 "into the land that I have given them."

688
00:27:59,660 --> 00:28:00,860
 This is unrighteous anger.

689
00:28:00,860 --> 00:28:03,000
 Why is that the case?

690
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:06,720
 Because Moses has had enough.

691
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:07,980
 He looks at the people,

692
00:28:07,980 --> 00:28:09,700
 and his patience has worn thin,

693
00:28:09,700 --> 00:28:12,020
 his fuse has burned up,

694
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:14,760
 he has grown annoyed as he has journeyed with them

695
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:16,020
 through the wilderness.

696
00:28:16,020 --> 00:28:18,460
 And yet, as he's done all of this,

697
00:28:18,460 --> 00:28:21,620
 it proves to us why he snaps in a given moment.

698
00:28:21,620 --> 00:28:22,840
 And it's this.

699
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:25,040
 Anger begins with legitimate frustration.

700
00:28:26,180 --> 00:28:29,880
 Anger always begins with legitimate frustration.

701
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:31,420
 Moses is legitimately frustrated.

702
00:28:31,420 --> 00:28:33,180
 He has spent, in this moment now,

703
00:28:33,180 --> 00:28:36,100
 almost 44 years in the desert with these people.

704
00:28:36,100 --> 00:28:39,800
 And that entire time, they have constantly grumbled,

705
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:41,260
 they have constantly complained,

706
00:28:41,260 --> 00:28:43,320
 they have personally attacked him,

707
00:28:43,320 --> 00:28:47,780
 they have only been a miserable party to road trip with.

708
00:28:47,780 --> 00:28:51,100
 And yet, he has been patient all the while

709
00:28:51,100 --> 00:28:52,420
 until this moment.

710
00:28:52,420 --> 00:28:54,020
 And yet, in this moment,

711
00:28:54,020 --> 00:28:56,460
 he gets frustrated enough under all of this

712
00:28:56,460 --> 00:28:59,980
 leadership fatigue, and he does what men do.

713
00:28:59,980 --> 00:29:01,780
 He explodes.

714
00:29:01,780 --> 00:29:03,420
 But here's the thing you need to know.

715
00:29:03,420 --> 00:29:05,580
 Men do not explode over one event.

716
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:08,940
 Men explode over the accumulation of several events.

717
00:29:08,940 --> 00:29:10,220
 I can take this thing now.

718
00:29:10,220 --> 00:29:12,420
 It's kind of like this.

719
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:14,020
 It's kind of like this Coke Zero.

720
00:29:14,020 --> 00:29:16,240
 Not regular Coke, 'cause Zoke is just better.

721
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:17,580
 Can we acknowledge that?

722
00:29:17,580 --> 00:29:18,840
 Zero calories, baby.

723
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:24,840
 The beauty of this is that it won't explode

724
00:29:24,840 --> 00:29:25,880
 under one event.

725
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:29,580
 But if she keeps nagging me,

726
00:29:29,580 --> 00:29:31,180
 and if they don't give me a break,

727
00:29:31,180 --> 00:29:33,300
 and if they only ever offer me feedback,

728
00:29:33,300 --> 00:29:36,500
 and if I just find that I'm never enough for these people,

729
00:29:36,500 --> 00:29:38,340
 and they keep grumbling against me,

730
00:29:38,340 --> 00:29:40,940
 and I'm gonna have to journey with them forever,

731
00:29:40,940 --> 00:29:42,740
 eventually the lid's gonna pop.

732
00:29:42,740 --> 00:29:47,380
 (congregation laughing)

733
00:29:47,380 --> 00:29:52,380
 And it's gonna make a mess of everyone and everything.

734
00:29:52,380 --> 00:29:57,300
 The difference between you and this Coke bottle

735
00:29:57,300 --> 00:29:59,200
 is some of you can't keep your lid on.

736
00:29:59,200 --> 00:30:05,820
 Because this we can control.

737
00:30:05,820 --> 00:30:09,740
 Some of you cannot control yourselves.

738
00:30:15,540 --> 00:30:18,300
 You need to also know that anger stems from entitlement.

739
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:21,620
 It's not something we struggle with, is it, guys?

740
00:30:21,620 --> 00:30:24,800
 Like, we never get annoyed

741
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:28,500
 because that person is sitting in the right turn lane,

742
00:30:28,500 --> 00:30:29,980
 but they're not choosing to turn right.

743
00:30:29,980 --> 00:30:31,540
 They're waiting to go straight.

744
00:30:31,540 --> 00:30:34,500
 It never frustrates us

745
00:30:34,500 --> 00:30:37,580
 that our friend happens to tell us the score of the game,

746
00:30:37,580 --> 00:30:39,180
 even though we're recording it at home,

747
00:30:39,180 --> 00:30:41,060
 and we plan to go zero dark 30

748
00:30:41,060 --> 00:30:43,560
 until that time when we can watch it by ourselves.

749
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:46,380
 This happens to us a lot.

750
00:30:46,380 --> 00:30:48,100
 We feel some sense of entitlement,

751
00:30:48,100 --> 00:30:51,260
 and because we are, we, like Moses,

752
00:30:51,260 --> 00:30:52,980
 we will represent our interest,

753
00:30:52,980 --> 00:30:55,620
 but as we do so, we will misrepresent the interest of God.

754
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:57,540
 That's what you do when you get angry.

755
00:30:57,540 --> 00:31:00,060
 Whenever your anger stems from entitlement,

756
00:31:00,060 --> 00:31:03,260
 you misrepresent who God is.

757
00:31:03,260 --> 00:31:04,100
 Look at me.

758
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:09,100
 Gentlemen, when you blow up, when you lose your cool,

759
00:31:09,100 --> 00:31:12,100
 when you say things you wish you could take back,

760
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:13,420
 but you know you cannot,

761
00:31:14,620 --> 00:31:16,260
 how is that representing God?

762
00:31:16,260 --> 00:31:19,180
 How is it representing Him?

763
00:31:19,180 --> 00:31:21,820
 Do people see you in that moment and think,

764
00:31:21,820 --> 00:31:24,300
 "God, He is so patient, and He is so gracious,

765
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:26,160
 "and He is so long-suffering,"

766
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:29,320
 or do they look at you and think,

767
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:30,680
 "That guy's got a temper.

768
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:33,580
 "I don't want anything to do with him.

769
00:31:33,580 --> 00:31:35,340
 "Who even invited him in the first place?"

770
00:31:35,340 --> 00:31:38,820
 Like, what is people's response to you?

771
00:31:38,820 --> 00:31:42,020
 When they respond to you in your fit of anger,

772
00:31:42,020 --> 00:31:45,360
 they are demonstrating some sense of response

773
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:47,420
 to your representation of God.

774
00:31:47,420 --> 00:31:51,620
 Who you are is about so much more than who you are.

775
00:31:51,620 --> 00:31:54,800
 It's about who He is, so check yourself.

776
00:31:54,800 --> 00:31:58,860
 And then lastly, anger can be costly.

777
00:31:58,860 --> 00:32:02,920
 It costs Moses the promised land,

778
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:04,900
 and it can cost us too.

779
00:32:04,900 --> 00:32:08,240
 Many men have lost their marriages.

780
00:32:08,240 --> 00:32:10,100
 They've lost a friend's trust.

781
00:32:10,100 --> 00:32:12,460
 They've lost their credibility at work.

782
00:32:12,460 --> 00:32:14,620
 They've lost a hard-earned reputation,

783
00:32:14,620 --> 00:32:16,420
 and they've lost decades of influence

784
00:32:16,420 --> 00:32:18,140
 because they reacted emotionally.

785
00:32:18,140 --> 00:32:21,180
 Hear me on this, guys.

786
00:32:21,180 --> 00:32:24,240
 How do you react whenever conflict arises?

787
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:27,180
 This will save you.

788
00:32:27,180 --> 00:32:29,420
 You do not gear up, you gear down.

789
00:32:29,420 --> 00:32:31,820
 I tell guys all the time,

790
00:32:31,820 --> 00:32:35,200
 you move through conflict in four-wheel drive.

791
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:38,860
 Oftentimes, men will do so in two-wheel drive,

792
00:32:38,860 --> 00:32:40,500
 that conflict is like mud.

793
